A CSS file's header comment is its first `/* */` comment, which only `@charset` may precede, even on its line; the header prints its first paragraph.
CSS has no doc comments, so any comment directly above a rule starts its line range, also inside an at-rule's block; a blank line detaches it, and a comment after a rule on its line belongs to that rule.
== args
input/buttons.css
== file input/buttons.css
@charset "UTF-8"; /*
 * Button styles.
 *
 * Shared by every page.
 */

/* Primary buttons. */
.primary {
  color: white;
}
.secondary {} /* Trailing note. */
.tertiary {}

/* Detached by a blank line. */

.link {}

@media print {
  /* Hidden when printed. */
  .primary {
    display: none;
  }
}
